    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Loading documents from Google Drive into Qdrant\n\nManual run → create the collection → fully clear the collection → list the files in the Google\nDrive folder → download → split into chunks and write to Qdrant.\n\n### What to replace before running\n\n- the Qdrant, Google Drive and OpenAI credentials: `YOUR_..._CREDENTIAL` is everywhere;\n- the \"Edit Fields\" node: `collection_name` and `qdrant_url` for your own instance;\n- the \"Get folder\" node: `YOUR_FOLDER_ID` to the ID of your own folder.\n\n### What to look at\n\nThe vector dimension in the body of the \"Create collection\" request (1536) is tied firmly to the embedding\nmodel: change the model and the collection has to be created anew. The \"Clear Collection\" node\nwipes the content entirely, so this is a full rebuild of the index, not an increment.\nThe incremental variant is in the example `m2-hybrid-search-record-manager.json`.",
        "height": 420,
        "width": 680,
        "color": 4
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -440,
        -500
      ],
      "id": "afff8480-5259-49ab-9265-aaa2f060ecb2",
      "name": "Sticky Note M2"
    }
  ],
